<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emil Körner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emil Körner was a Prussian army officer hired by Chile in 1885 to modernise its army. He reformed military education and organisation on German lines, and during the civil war of 1891 he sided with Congress and helped plan its victory over President Balmaceda. As chief of the general staff he completed the Prussianisation of the Chilean army before retiring in 1910.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emil-korner.jpg" alt="Emil Körner" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emil_K%C3%B6rner_Ej%C3%A9rcito_Chile.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
